; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; What the Huntress moves by -- the Rogue, drawn as neilhancart's "Huntress".
;
; Her skeleton is not the kit's. The Humanoid set's clips are KayKit's and drive
; KayKit bones (hips, upperarm.l); hers is a Maya HumanIK rig
; (QuickRigCharacter_Hips_03 ...), so not one of them would reach her and she
; would stand in her A-pose. The clips the Rogue's block names are therefore
; retargeted onto her own bones once, in Blender (art/huntress/export_huntress.py),
; and written here under the KayKit names -- so his block names them exactly as
; it did.
;
; ★ STAND-INS. These are the KayKit movements on her body, not movements made for
; her: a chibi's bow stance on a grown woman. When a library on her own skeleton
; arrives (Quaternius' Universal Animation Library is the plan), it is a second
; line under Libraries and a word per clip in rogue.duke.
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
AnimationSet
  Name = Huntress
  Libraries = [
    animations/characters/huntress.glb,
  ]
  Idle = Ranged_Bow_Idle
  Walk = Running_A
  Attack = Ranged_Bow_Release
  Death = Death_A
End
